{"name":"Life Is Good","hex":"#e19b42","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"life","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of organisms preceding their death, characterized by biological processes such as metabolism and reproduction and distinguishing them from inanimate objects; the state of being alive and living.","The status possessed by any of a number of entities, including animals, plants, fungi, bacteria, and sometimes viruses, which have the properties of replication and metabolism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To replace components whose operational lifetime has expired."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/life"},{"term":"good","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person or an animal:\nActing in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral.","Acting in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good"}],"entries":[{"title":"Life Is Good (Emilio album)","blocks":[{"text":"Life Is Good is the first country music album by American Tejano music artist Emilio Navaira. It was released by Capitol Nashville on September 26, 1995. Its first single, \"It's Not the End of the World,\" reached the Top 30 on the Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart. The album peaked at #13 on the Top Country Albums chart and #82 on the Billboard 200."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/LifeIsGoodEmilio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_Is_Good_(Emilio_album)","wikidata":"Q6544864"},{"title":"Life Is Good (Flogging Molly album)","blocks":[{"text":"Life Is Good is the sixth studio album by the Irish-American Celtic punk band Flogging Molly, released on June 2, 2017. Their first studio album in six years, it is also their first album to feature drummer Mike Alonso, and their last album with banjo player Bob Schmidt."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Life_is_Good_Flogging_Molly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_Is_Good_(Flogging_Molly_album)","wikidata":"Q30610067"},{"title":"Life Is Good (Nas album)","blocks":[{"text":"Life Is Good is the tenth studio album by the American rapper Nas, released on July 13, 2012, by the Jones Experience and Def Jam Recordings. The album was recorded at various studios in New York and California, with guest appearances from rappers Large Professor and Rick Ross, and singers Mary J. Blige, Miguel, and, posthumously, Amy Winehouse, among others."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5c/Nas_-_Life_is_Good.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_Is_Good_(Nas_album)","wikidata":"Q2701394"},{"title":"Life","blocks":[{"text":"Life is the capacity in matter, formed of one or more units called cells, for processes such as cell signalling, homeostasis, metabolism, cell growth, adaptation, response to stimuli, and reproduction. All life eventually reaches a state of death. Many philosophical definitions of living systems have been proposed, such as self-organising systems. Defining life is further complicated by viruses, which replicate only in host cells, and the possibility of extraterrestrial life, which could be very different from life on Earth. Life exists all over the Earth in air, water, and soil, with many ecosystems forming the biosphere. Some of these are harsh environments occupied only by extremophiles. The life in a particular ecosystem is called its biota."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg/330px-Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life","wikidata":"Q3"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Kelis_1.jpg/500px-Kelis_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Kelis_1.jpg/1280px-Kelis_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Kelis_1.jpg/500px-Kelis_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nas' divorce from singer Kelis (photographed in 2010) inspired much of the album.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKelis_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Nas_Life_is_Good_release_party.jpg/500px-Nas_Life_is_Good_release_party.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Nas_Life_is_Good_release_party.jpg/1280px-Nas_Life_is_Good_release_party.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Nas_Life_is_Good_release_party.jpg/500px-Nas_Life_is_Good_release_party.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nas performing in July 2012 at the release party for Life Is Good","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANas_Life_is_Good_release_party.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/500px-Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Male_Lion_and_Cub_Chitwa_South_Africa_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/1280px-Male_Lion_and